# Repository-root ignores.
#
# windows/.gitignore already covers the .NET build artifacts, the vendored
# llama.cpp runtime and the GGUF model, and it stays the owner of those. This
# file covers the repository root, which had no .gitignore at all.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party adventure material.
#
# Reference modules are read locally while authoring a campaign; none of them
# may be committed. This repository publishes a public installer and is kept
# deliberately clean against SRD 5.2.1, and the material that gets dropped here
# generally is not: fan modules built on a commercial setting carry the setting
# owner's trademarks and artwork, and cite creatures by Monster Manual page
# rather than from the SRD. A fan author cannot license a setting they do not
# own, so their permission would not cover it either.
#
# Keep the source documents local, ship only original, SRD-derived campaigns.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sample Campaigns/*
!Sample Campaigns/.gitkeep
!Sample Campaigns/README.md

*.pdf
*.epub
*.mobi
*.docx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent worktrees.
#
# .claude/worktrees/ holds complete git checkouts of this repository, one per
# parallel track. Committing it would nest the repository inside itself.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor noise. desktop.ini matters here specifically because the
# working copy lives inside a OneDrive folder, which writes them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Scratch space
scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp
